1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,580
This tiny machine beats 28,800 times an hour,

2
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:06,072
and it’s never once needed a battery.

3
00:00:06,672 --> 00:00:08,352
It’s calibre 3235,

4
00:00:08,102 --> 00:00:11,212
the beating heart of a modern Rolex.

5
00:00:10,962 --> 00:00:12,532
So let’s turn it over,

6
00:00:12,282 --> 00:00:13,193
open it up,

7
00:00:12,943 --> 00:00:14,153
and have a look.

8
00:00:16,453 --> 00:00:18,861
Every move of your wrist swings the rotor,

9
00:00:18,611 --> 00:00:20,249
which winds the mainspring,

10
00:00:19,999 --> 00:00:23,178
storing about seventy hours of power in this little drum.

11
00:00:24,478 --> 00:00:26,610
The gear train counts the time out,

12
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,222
and the escapement lets it go,

13
00:00:27,972 --> 00:00:29,458
half a tooth at a time.

14
00:00:29,208 --> 00:00:30,728
Lock, release, impulse.

15
00:00:30,478 --> 00:00:32,134
That’s the tick you hear.

16
00:00:33,335 --> 00:00:35,769
And keeping it all in time is the balance,

17
00:00:35,519 --> 00:00:38,317
swinging four times a second on a blue hairspring

18
00:00:38,067 --> 00:00:39,617
of niobium and zirconium.

19
00:00:40,116 --> 00:00:41,686
Want the full breakdown?

20
00:00:41,436 --> 00:00:43,687
It’s waiting on the channel.

